fix: retry the fetch
EOF
)", git commit -sm "$(cat <<'EOF'
docs: describe the checkout step
EOF
)", git commit -qam "... keep main green ...", and git add -A && git commit -am "$(cat <<'EOF'
chore: branch cleanup
EOF
)". git commit -am is an ordinary builder form. (2) No test decides that free-text values stay out of the position test's scan: making _segment_chunks keep them fails none of test_merge_guard (34 passed), because every tested heredoc message is upgraded to the plain path first. The behaviour is right today (FOO=$HOME git commit -m 'fix: retry the fetch' passes in the worktree) but unguarded.
